body.br:
SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.150.227

1.    (Currently Amended) A lancing device for use with a disposable lancet having a lancet body and a sharp lancet tip for penetrating skin, comprising:

a housing defining a cavity;

a lancet carrier positioned within the cavity, the lancet carrier being configured to releasably engage a disposable lancet, the lancet carrier being movable in a direction along a lancing stroke from a retracted position to an extended position where at least the sharp lancet tip of the disposable lancet is configured to project[[s]] out from the housing;

a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier from the extended position to a neutral position;

a drive spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier along an advancing portion of the lancing stroke from the retracted position to the extended position;

a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier from the extended position to a neutral position;

a latch mechanism operable to permit the lancet carrier to travel through the advancing portion and the return portion of the lancing stroke, and to thereafter prevent excess oscillation of the lancet carrier from the neutral position;

a removable cap positionable over a distal end of the housing, wherein removal of the cap from the housing allows access to the cavity in order to remove and replace the disposable lancet; and

an ejection member having an ejection finger and an extension, the ejection member being movable distally to eject the disposable lancet from the lancet carrier, wherein at least portions of both the ejection finger and the extension extend along the direction of the lancing stroke, the extension extending distally beyond the ejection finger, wherein the ejection finger is configured to contact the proximal end of the disposable lancet.

2.
(Currently Amended) The lancing device of claim 1, wherein the ejection finger is configured to eject[[s]] the disposable lancet when the ejection member moves distally.



3.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 2, wherein the extension bears against the removable cap when the cap is positioned over the distal end of the housing.



4.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 3, wherein the ejection finger of the ejection member comprises a portion that extends generally along the direction of the lancing stroke and a portion that extends generally in a direction perpendicular to the direction of the lancing stroke.



5.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 3, wherein the ejection finger of the ejection member has a surface defining a plane perpendicular to the direction of the lancing stroke.



6.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 1, wherein the ejection finger and extension are unitary with the ejection member.



7.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim   1, wherein the ejection member is moveable separately from the lancet carrier.





8.    (Currently Amended) A lancing device for use with a disposable lancet having a lancet body and a sharp lancet tip for penetrating skin, comprising:

a housing defining a cavity;

a lancet carrier positioned within the cavity, the lancet carrier being configured to releasably engage a disposable lancet, the lancet carrier being movable in a direction along a lancing stroke from a retracted position to an extended position where at least the sharp lancet tip of the disposable lancet is configured to project[[s]] out from the housing;

a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier from the extended position to a neutral position;

a drive spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier along an advancing portion of the lancing stroke from the retracted position to the extended position;

a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier along a return portion of the lancing stroke from the extended position to a neutral position;

a latch mechanism operable to permit the lancet carrier to travel through the advancing portion and the return portion of the lancing stroke, and to thereafter prevent excess oscillation of the lancet carrier from the neutral position;

a removable cap positionable over a distal end of the housing, wherein removal of the cap from the housing allows access to the cavity in order to remove and replace the disposable lancet; and

an ejection member having an ejection finger and an extension, the ejection member being movable distally wherein the ejection finger is configured to eject the disposable lancet from the lancet carrier,

the lancet carrier having a slot, the ejection finger extending through the slot to contact a proximal end of the disposable lancet, the extension extending along the direction of the lancing stroke distally beyond the ejection finger.



9.    (Currently Amended) The lancing device of claim 8, wherein the ejection finger ejects is configured to eject the disposable lancet when the ejection member moves distally.



10.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 9, wherein the extension bears against the removable cap when the cap is positioned over the distal end of the housing.



11.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 10, wherein the ejection finger of the ejection member comprises a portion that extends generally along the direction of the lancing stroke and a portion that extends generally in a direction perpendicular to the direction of the lancing stroke.



12.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 10, wherein the ejection finger of the ejection member has a surface defining a plane perpendicular to the direction of the lancing stroke.



13.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 8, wherein the ejection finger and extension are unitary with the ejection member.



14.    (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim  8, wherein the ejection member is moveable separately from the lancet carrier.



15.    (Currently Amended) A lancing device for use with a disposable lancet having a lancet body and a sharp lancet tip for penetrating skin, comprising:

a housing defining a cavity;

a lancet carrier positioned within the cavity, the lancet carrier having a slot and being configured to releasably engage a disposable lancet, the lancet carrier being movable in a



direction along a lancing stroke from a retracted position to an extended position where at least the sharp lancet tip of the disposable lancet is configured to project[[s]] out from the housing;a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier from the extended position to a neutral position;

a drive spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier along an advancing portion of the lancing stroke from the retracted position to the extended position;

a return spring positioned within the cavity and configured to propel the lancet carrier along a return portion of the lancing stroke from the extended position to a neutral position;

a latch mechanism operable to permit the lancet carrier to travel through the advancing portion and the return portion of the lancing stroke, and to thereafter prevent excess oscillation of the lancet carrier from the neutral position;

a removable cap positionable over a distal end of the housing, wherein removal of the cap from the housing allows access to the cavity in order to remove and replace the disposable lancet;

an ejection member having an ejection finger and an extension, the ejection finger extending through the slot to contact the disposable lancet at a proximal end and the ejection member being movable distally to eject the disposable lancet from the lancet carrier, the extension extending along the direction of the lancing stroke distally beyond the ejection finger;

and a button operably connected to the lancet carrier and configured to hold the lancet carrier in the retracted position and, when pressed, to release the lancet carrier and to allow the lancet carrier to move from the retracted position to the extended position.





16.   (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 15, further comprising a slide operably connected to the lancet carrier and adapted to move the lancet carrier from the neutral position to the retracted position to energize the drive spring.



17.   (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim   15, wherein the ejection member is moveable separately from the lancet carrier.



18.   (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 19, wherein the ejection finger of the ejection member has a surface defining a plane perpendicular to the direction of the lancing stroke.



19.   (Previously Presented) The lancing device of claim 15, wherein the ejection finger and extension are unitary with the ejection member.
